WEBVTT

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.733
<i>What's this feeling I have,</i>
<i>as if I'm looking forward to...</i>

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:25.939
<i>... somebody firing off his</i>
<i>missiles and ending everything?</i>

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:31.378
<i>Is it a bad thing, or is this normal?</i>

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:37.884
<i>I can't figure it out on my</i>
<i>own, so somebody tell me!</i>

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:43.490
<i>And that person I love has once again...</i>

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>... gone far away without anybody noticing.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:56.103
<i>Where have my dreams gone since then?</i>

00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:01.775
<i>I could swear that they</i>
<i>were right here long ago.</i>

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:07.814
<i>We had a love that set our hearts on fire.</i>

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:20.784
<i>Let's take back that feeling we had back then!</i>

00:02:11.378 --> 00:02:13.175
I'm bored of this.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.183
Precious metals and jewels, beautiful dresses,

00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:19.519
and enough booze to
last me 'til my dying day...

00:02:19.519 --> 00:02:22.122
It's all so pointless.

00:02:22.122 --> 00:02:25.859
Something's... Something's missing.

00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:29.763
Tell me you're not about to say "love."

00:02:29.763 --> 00:02:31.628
Get real.

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.903
Where are you going?

00:02:36.903 --> 00:02:39.072
For a walk.

00:02:39.072 --> 00:02:40.774
Can I come with you?

00:02:40.774 --> 00:02:42.742
Don't follow me.

00:02:45.912 --> 00:02:49.370
Don't get cocky, you self-centered woman...

00:03:01.194 --> 00:03:04.231
Three unexplained luminescent
phenomena such as this

00:03:04.231 --> 00:03:07.334
have been spotted in
three locations around Tokyo.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:12.072
The current opinion, that they are
plasma luminescence, has some validity,

00:03:12.072 --> 00:03:17.203
- but they may be a mermaid...
- There some weird things
in the world, huh, Sakuya?

00:03:21.281 --> 00:03:24.184
Hey, Sakuya! How about breakfast?

00:03:24.184 --> 00:03:27.187
I'll put everything I've learned
from living by myself into it!

00:03:27.187 --> 00:03:29.212
Stay with me...

00:03:30.824 --> 00:03:35.124
Please... Don't leave me alone...

00:03:36.263 --> 00:03:41.768
She showed up of a sudden yesterday,
and she's been like this all night.

00:03:41.768 --> 00:03:43.929
What the heck happened?

00:03:53.947 --> 00:03:56.850
Ah, busy, busy, busy...

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:01.810
I must lay more traps around the
house and strengthen our defenses!

00:04:09.262 --> 00:04:11.253
Yugi...

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:18.972
Busy, busy, busy...

00:04:18.972 --> 00:04:21.497
Honestly, this is all too much...

00:04:23.443 --> 00:04:26.435
Sasami? Don't cut your fingers, okay?

00:04:40.927 --> 00:04:43.830
What a surprise!

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:48.164
To think that a gem like this
had such a secret hidden inside it...

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:52.439
And now, the next order of business.

00:04:52.439 --> 00:04:55.742
Sakuya Kumashiro, now it's your turn.

00:04:55.742 --> 00:04:59.646
To prove my theory, I'll use this,
invented by L'il Washu,

00:04:59.646 --> 00:05:02.882
the greatest scientific genius in the galaxy.

00:05:02.882 --> 00:05:05.485
The 2nd-generation
"Mr. Surveillance" style sensor mecha,

00:05:05.485 --> 00:05:07.487
which I call "Mr. Analysis."

00:05:07.487 --> 00:05:10.820
I'm gonna use this to
find out who you really are.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.660
Analyze! Analyze!

00:05:26.673 --> 00:05:33.613
He didn't have to pick a planet
like this to build a hideout...

00:05:33.613 --> 00:05:38.915
Oh, well. Nobody can come here,
so it'll make a good hideout, anyway.

00:05:43.957 --> 00:05:45.652
Love, huh?

00:05:53.466 --> 00:05:55.457
Okay, one more time!

00:06:06.012 --> 00:06:08.810
And this goes here...

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.218
Hey, not too shabby.

00:06:12.218 --> 00:06:14.587
I bet Sasami'd love this if she saw it.

00:06:14.587 --> 00:06:18.525
And I know that Mihoshi
would do something like this.

00:06:18.525 --> 00:06:22.629
"Policeman, help me! I'm gonna be eaten!"

00:06:22.629 --> 00:06:24.961
"It's cold!"

00:06:31.738 --> 00:06:35.141
What the heck am I doing?

00:06:35.141 --> 00:06:37.507
Maybe I'll go back to the hideout.

00:06:40.847 --> 00:06:46.753
It was Hotsuma who found
this planet and built our hideout.

00:06:46.753 --> 00:06:51.087
Whatever else you can say about
the guy, he's sure done a lot for me.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.934
I'm freezing! I gotta get warmed up soon...

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:05.303
I had prepared myself, but
I didn't think it would be this bad.

00:07:06.573 --> 00:07:09.676
All she thinks about is
money, drinking, and destruction.

00:07:09.676 --> 00:07:14.013
She acts like an animal!
No, worse than an animal!

00:07:14.013 --> 00:07:16.382
She's decided that we're friends,

00:07:16.382 --> 00:07:19.452
but I'm not the least bit interested
in that self-centered woman!

00:07:19.452 --> 00:07:21.855
And I'm sick of looking at her!

00:07:21.855 --> 00:07:25.518
At any rate, I'm fed up with
being Ryoko's nursemaid!

00:07:27.293 --> 00:07:29.591
Hotsuma!

00:07:38.705 --> 00:07:41.474
Damn. You, too, huh?

00:07:41.474 --> 00:07:45.678
Forget it. I give up. It's stupid.

00:07:45.678 --> 00:07:47.543
Who's there?

00:07:51.885 --> 00:07:54.254
It couldn't be... Ryoko?

00:07:54.254 --> 00:07:57.290
She overheard us?

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.781
Looks like this little game is over.

00:08:01.227 --> 00:08:02.729
Shall I kill her?

00:08:02.729 --> 00:08:04.030
I suppose so.

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.691
Yes, Ma'am.

00:08:09.869 --> 00:08:12.872
I have to go to my training soon.

00:08:12.872 --> 00:08:16.609
It's nothing fancy, but since
I made breakfast, let's eat together.

00:08:16.609 --> 00:08:18.099
Okay?

00:08:20.246 --> 00:08:23.316
I don't understand that girl anymore.

00:08:23.316 --> 00:08:25.919
It's almost time, I suppose.

00:08:25.919 --> 00:08:28.755
Tsugaru, I'll need your help.

00:08:28.755 --> 00:08:30.120
Understood.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:40.861
Analyze this! Analyze that! Analyze, analyze!

00:08:42.836 --> 00:08:47.273
Looking good, Mr. Analysis!
Keep sending me more data!

00:08:47.273 --> 00:08:49.969
More data on Sakuya Kumashiro!

00:09:02.655 --> 00:09:04.646
This feels great...

00:09:09.295 --> 00:09:14.033
I really didn't think of
anything but running wild.

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:18.938
All I did was drink and shut people
up because I was so full of myself.

00:09:18.938 --> 00:09:24.777
But I... I don't wanna
hear it from a guy like you,

00:09:24.777 --> 00:09:27.109
from a guy like you who
complains behind my back!

00:09:58.244 --> 00:09:59.612
Damn it!

00:09:59.612 --> 00:10:01.546
This just ticks me off!

00:10:07.387 --> 00:10:10.254
I look so pathetic...

00:10:16.429 --> 00:10:18.260
Tenchi...

00:10:30.243 --> 00:10:33.235
Maybe I'll go back to Okayama.

00:10:45.825 --> 00:10:47.894
Bye, Hotsuma.

00:10:47.894 --> 00:10:49.062
Gai'en! Let me in!

00:10:49.062 --> 00:10:50.586
Yes, Sir!

00:10:59.806 --> 00:11:01.933
Goodbye, Ryoko.

00:11:04.177 --> 00:11:05.838
Oh, damn!

00:11:10.183 --> 00:11:13.516
Now that weight's finally off my shoulders.

00:11:33.873 --> 00:11:37.543
We've entered the
Saturn area of the Sol system.

00:11:37.543 --> 00:11:40.646
It's not much further to Earth.

00:11:40.646 --> 00:11:42.841
But still...

00:11:45.251 --> 00:11:47.186
Mihoshi! Have you found it?

00:11:47.186 --> 00:11:51.924
No! I haven't found it yet!

00:11:51.924 --> 00:11:54.560
If you don't find it, I'm not
taking you down to Earth!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.129
I hope you understand that!

00:11:56.129 --> 00:11:59.098
Ow! You're kidding!

00:11:59.098 --> 00:12:01.667
Not only that, I'll throw you into space

00:12:01.667 --> 00:12:05.104
and give Earth a new satellite!

00:12:05.104 --> 00:12:06.773
I'm sorry!

00:12:06.773 --> 00:12:09.242
Tenchi!

00:12:09.242 --> 00:12:14.145
Of all the... How could she
lose the gem that Tenchi gave her?

00:12:18.651 --> 00:12:22.455
I feel like I'm coming back home
after being away for a long time.

00:12:22.455 --> 00:12:25.515
It's... It's kind of strange.

00:12:38.438 --> 00:12:40.706
That's that.

00:12:40.706 --> 00:12:43.766
Goodbye, Sakuya.

00:12:49.282 --> 00:12:54.049
Sakuya... I wonder if she's okay?

00:12:57.156 --> 00:13:00.193
Anyway, I'd better finish up
here quickly and head back home.

00:13:00.193 --> 00:13:02.261
Hey, Masaki!

00:13:02.261 --> 00:13:04.430
Hey, Tsuchida. Hey, Amagasaki.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:08.167
It's finally summer vacation, and
here you are, working your tail off...

00:13:08.167 --> 00:13:10.403
It's his training, so I guess
he doesn't have any choice.

00:13:10.403 --> 00:13:15.274
We're on our way over to
the pool for a quick swim!

00:13:15.274 --> 00:13:16.876
I bet you're jealous.

00:13:16.876 --> 00:13:18.111
Yeah.

00:13:18.111 --> 00:13:21.280
It seems kinda pathetic
with just us guys going, though.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.051
What're you talking about?
It's more than Masaki's got.

00:13:25.051 --> 00:13:29.511
He's so busy training that he doesn't
even have time to get a girlfriend.

00:13:30.456 --> 00:13:32.458
Even if they're not your girlfriends,

00:13:32.458 --> 00:13:35.962
it'd be nice if you could
get yourself some girl friends.

00:13:35.962 --> 00:13:39.866
Hey... What're you two saying?

00:13:39.866 --> 00:13:44.670
What do you mean?
You should make some girl friends...

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.305
Wait a minute! You...

00:13:46.305 --> 00:13:49.175
A-Are you saying that
you've got a girlfriend?!

00:13:49.175 --> 00:13:51.711
Who is she?! Tell us! Tell us!

00:13:51.711 --> 00:13:56.349
What do you mean, "Who?"
It's Sakuya Kumashiro.

00:13:56.349 --> 00:13:58.151
- Sakuya Kumashiro?!
- Sakuya Kumashiro?!

00:13:58.151 --> 00:14:00.119
Does she go to our school?!

00:14:00.119 --> 00:14:01.387
What year is she?! What class?!

00:14:01.387 --> 00:14:04.991
What're you talking about? She's in our class.

00:14:04.991 --> 00:14:07.755
She went to the beach
with us a while ago, remember?

00:14:21.574 --> 00:14:25.011
Hey. Stop screwing around.

00:14:25.011 --> 00:14:27.146
Stop teasing me.

00:14:27.146 --> 00:14:31.918
All of us did go to the
beach a while ago... Right?

00:14:31.918 --> 00:14:37.323
Yeah. But there wasn't
anybody there named Kumashiro.

00:14:37.323 --> 00:14:38.958
Are you okay, Masaki?

00:14:38.958 --> 00:14:41.827
You haven't been out in
the sun too long, have you?

00:14:41.827 --> 00:14:44.625
There wasn't anybody there named Kumashiro!

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.635
Sakuya?

00:14:49.635 --> 00:14:51.500
Sakuya!

00:14:53.806 --> 00:14:56.108
Hey! What's wrong, Masaki?!

00:14:56.108 --> 00:14:58.678
Masaki!

00:14:58.678 --> 00:15:00.513
What's with him?

00:15:00.513 --> 00:15:02.315
That's one strange guy.

00:15:02.315 --> 00:15:04.016
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:15:04.016 --> 00:15:05.608
Sakuya!

00:15:09.989 --> 00:15:11.958
Darn it... Darn it...

00:15:11.958 --> 00:15:12.758
Darn it...

00:15:12.758 --> 00:15:14.555
Ow!

00:15:20.766 --> 00:15:23.135
That'll do it.

00:15:23.135 --> 00:15:25.705
Okay, here goes.

00:15:25.705 --> 00:15:30.404
If I apply my Washu Special
bio-wave filter to this image...

00:15:34.313 --> 00:15:36.148
As I thought.

00:15:36.148 --> 00:15:39.709
Sakuya Kumashiro, she...

00:15:42.288 --> 00:15:44.188
Sakuya!

00:15:49.428 --> 00:15:52.727
Maybe she went home. I'll try her place.

00:15:57.803 --> 00:15:59.138
There it is!

00:15:59.138 --> 00:16:00.706
Sakuya Kumashiro!

00:16:00.706 --> 00:16:02.708
See? She's in here!

00:16:02.708 --> 00:16:05.939
Tsuchida and Amagasaki
were just messing with me!

00:16:20.593 --> 00:16:24.463
It serves her right... It's over, Yugi.

00:16:24.463 --> 00:16:26.666
I wish I could've done this right away,

00:16:26.666 --> 00:16:29.464
instead of resorting to all these cheap tricks.

00:16:32.204 --> 00:16:34.573
So that's it.

00:16:34.573 --> 00:16:39.779
You suckered me and dragged
me out to this backwater planet.

00:16:39.779 --> 00:16:42.948
You separated Tenchi and me...

00:16:42.948 --> 00:16:45.439
What're you up to?!

00:16:58.564 --> 00:17:03.331
How? How did you survive that explosion?!

00:17:05.504 --> 00:17:07.707
It's because of this.

00:17:07.707 --> 00:17:12.144
I realized that I'd forgotten
it, so I went back for it.

00:17:12.144 --> 00:17:14.780
A picture? Pathetic.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.416
It may be pathetic to you,

00:17:17.416 --> 00:17:21.987
but to me, it's almost
as important as life itself.

00:17:21.987 --> 00:17:25.787
Tenchi... Tenchi saved me.

00:17:28.294 --> 00:17:32.498
It's hopeless! He belongs
to another woman now!

00:17:32.498 --> 00:17:37.503
Ryoko, no matter how much
you love him, he won't fall for you!

00:17:37.503 --> 00:17:40.506
That doesn't matter.

00:17:40.506 --> 00:17:44.043
No, that doesn't matter at all.

00:17:44.043 --> 00:17:49.749
Because I've realized how I really feel.

00:17:49.749 --> 00:17:52.318
How you really feel?

00:17:52.318 --> 00:17:55.121
I love Tenchi.

00:17:55.121 --> 00:17:57.123
Nothing else matters.

00:17:57.123 --> 00:18:02.928
It's enough that I have
my love for Tenchi right here.

00:18:02.928 --> 00:18:03.596
What the...?

00:18:03.596 --> 00:18:05.223
You're wide open!

00:18:08.934 --> 00:18:10.492
Don't tell me...

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.435
Something's happened to Tenchi?!

00:18:18.778 --> 00:18:20.370
What the...?

00:18:26.485 --> 00:18:28.454
Huh?

00:18:28.454 --> 00:18:32.425
Wait, is that... Could it be?

00:18:32.425 --> 00:18:34.727
Found it!

00:18:34.727 --> 00:18:37.594
But why's it glowing?

00:18:39.899 --> 00:18:41.801
It's...

00:18:41.801 --> 00:18:43.736
Something's happening on Earth?

00:18:43.736 --> 00:18:45.363
Let's move it!

00:18:49.208 --> 00:18:50.976
Sister!

00:18:50.976 --> 00:18:53.342
Sister! My gem, it's...

00:18:56.849 --> 00:18:58.840
What's that?

00:19:05.391 --> 00:19:06.722
That's...

00:19:07.259 --> 00:19:10.629
If we don't do something
about this, and soon,

00:19:10.629 --> 00:19:12.290
we're in trouble.

00:19:16.235 --> 00:19:17.603
I won't let you go back to Earth!

00:19:17.603 --> 00:19:18.838
Say what?

00:19:18.838 --> 00:19:20.473
You'll die here!

00:19:20.473 --> 00:19:22.373
Shove it!

00:19:24.109 --> 00:19:27.636
Now entering atmosphere!
Heading straight for Okayama!

00:19:33.819 --> 00:19:35.120
What was that?

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:38.390
We've been attacked by
something! Damage is extensive!

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:40.259
We're gonna crash!

00:19:40.259 --> 00:19:43.057
Attacked by what?!

00:19:51.303 --> 00:19:53.405
All right, then...

00:19:53.405 --> 00:19:56.609
If I add in the bio-wave data
we took from Yugi in that fight

00:19:56.609 --> 00:19:59.169
to the filter and overlay it right here...

00:20:02.882 --> 00:20:08.554
No doubt about it.
Sakuya Kumashiro is Yugi's alter-ego.

00:20:08.554 --> 00:20:14.186
An apparition created by
Yugi that doesn't really exist.

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:26.465
This is the place.

00:20:30.709 --> 00:20:34.113
Sakuya! It's me! It's Masaki!

00:20:34.113 --> 00:20:36.849
Sakuya!

00:20:36.849 --> 00:20:39.079
I'm coming in, Sakuya!

00:20:47.526 --> 00:20:49.494
S-Sakuya...

00:20:56.368 --> 00:21:01.140
No... I hate being alone!

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:05.277
Tenchi! I'm scared!

00:21:05.277 --> 00:21:07.177
Tenchi!

00:21:36.241 --> 00:21:39.845
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:39.845 --> 00:21:43.749
<i>Sleeping late, staying up late,</i>
<i>and napping all the time!</i>

00:21:43.749 --> 00:21:47.353
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:47.353 --> 00:21:51.290
<i>Sneaking bites to eat, midnight</i>
<i>snacks, and pouring tea on my rice!</i>

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:54.793
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:54.793 --> 00:21:58.764
<i>Playing video games and singing karaoke!</i>

00:21:58.764 --> 00:22:02.101
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:22:02.101 --> 00:22:06.105
<i>Lying in the sun and taking baths outside!</i>

00:22:06.105 --> 00:22:08.240
<i>- Taking side trips!</i>
<i>- Gossiping!</i>

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:10.175
<i>- Taking long baths</i>
<i>- Wasting my money!</i>

00:22:10.175 --> 00:22:11.677
<i>- Being a busybody!</i>
<i>- Talking forever on the phone!</i>

00:22:11.677 --> 00:22:17.516
<i>- Unrequited love!</i>
<i>- Stealing other people's men!</i>

00:22:17.516 --> 00:22:21.620
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:24.890
<i>no matter how old I get!</i>

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:28.427
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:28.427 --> 00:22:33.126
<i>even if I die, change shape, or get reborn!</i>

00:22:44.476 --> 00:22:47.479
Hello, Sakuya? It's Tenchi.

00:22:47.479 --> 00:22:50.182
I'm not calling for any particular reason,

00:22:50.182 --> 00:22:53.819
but you've looked kind of depressed lately.

00:22:53.819 --> 00:22:58.257
If you want, I thought that maybe
we could do something tomorrow.

00:22:58.257 --> 00:23:04.263
I may not be able to do much,
but I'd like to help you, Sakuya.

00:23:04.263 --> 00:23:11.328
Next time on <i>Tenchi in Tokyo:</i>
"Yugi's Shadow."
